Bundled data sources and their licences are listed below as they are added.
Each entry names the source, its date or version, and its licence.

E-Bilanz-Taxonomie 6.9 position identifiers (templates/de-hgb.toml)
  Position identifiers of the German E-Bilanz taxonomy, version 6.9,
  published with the BMF letter of 10 June 2025 (EStH, Anhang 7) and used
  for ELSTER interoperability. Taxonomy © XBRL Deutschland e.V.,
  https://www.xbrl.de / https://de.xbrl.org. Only the identifiers are
  bundled, no taxonomy text. Per https://de.xbrl.org/disclaimer/, use
  including commercial use is permitted provided the copyright notice is
  retained.

SKR03/SKR04 mapping numbers (templates/mappings/)
  Bare DATEV Standardkontenrahmen account numbers used as the
  industry-standard interchange interface for German bookkeeping exports.
  No DATEV account names or other DATEV texts are bundled ("Nachdruck -
  auch auszugsweise - nicht gestattet"); see templates/LICENSES.md.

ISO 4217 currency table (crates/ledgers-money/src/currency.rs)
  Active and historic ISO 4217 currency codes with numeric codes and
  decimal exponents. Primary source: Wikipedia, ISO 4217 article
  (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217), retrieved 2026-10-18.
  Only the alphabetic codes, numeric codes, and exponents (facts, not
  copyrightable) are bundled; no Wikipedia article text (which carries
  CC BY-SA 4.0) is included. Secondary source and cross-check:
  datasets/currency-codes (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasets/
  currency-codes/master/data/codes-all.csv), which mirrors the ISO 4217
  maintenance-agency data under the Open Data Commons Public Domain
  Dedication and Licence (ODC-PDDL).

Data file licences (templates/LICENSES.md)
  Per-file licence index of every bundled template file, including charts,
  mappings, and translations. See templates/LICENSES.md for details.
  Ledgers' own templates are licensed under MIT (repository licence).

German statutory tax rates (crates/ledgers-tax/src/rate.rs)
  German VAT rates (Umsatzsteuer, §12 UStG) with effective date ranges.
  Bundled standard and reduced rates: 19%/7% (2007–2020-06-30, 2021–open),
  16%/5% temporary reduction (2020-07-01–2020-12-31 per Zweites Corona-
  Steuerhilfegesetz, BGBl. I 2020 S. 1512), and 0% zero rate (2007–open).
  Rates are public domain per §5 UrhG (German Copyright Act).

E-invoice and e-filing samples
  No e-invoice samples (XRechnung, ZUGFeRD) are bundled. Test fixtures
  use invented company names (e.g., Halden Works GmbH, Acme GmbH).
